---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import ConnectsStrip from '../components/ConnectsStrip.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import Fig2ThreadDiagram from '../components/Fig2ThreadDiagram.astro';
import StepRow from '../components/StepRow.astro';
import ServiceList from '../components/ServiceList.astro';
import ProductGrid from '../components/ProductGrid.astro';
import Specimen from '../components/Specimen.astro';
import ContactSection from '../components/ContactSection.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Base>
  <Header />
  <Hero />
  <ConnectsStrip />

  <Section
    eyebrow="§ 01 — The problem"
    heading="Nothing is broken. That’s the problem."
    headingWidth={16}
    headingGap={24}
    noteLabel="Typical intake"
  >
    <p class="txt" style="margin-bottom:16px">
      Every tool you bought works. QuickBooks does accounting. Square takes payments. The
      scheduling app schedules. Each one is fine on its own, and none of them know the
      others exist.
    </p>
    <p class="txt" style="margin-bottom:16px">
      So a person becomes the integration. Someone reads a number off one screen and types
      it into another. Someone checks four tabs to answer one question. Someone remembers
      to send the invoice. It never shows up as a line item, which is exactly why it never
      gets fixed.
    </p>
    <p class="txt">That work is the thing we remove.</p>

    <Fragment slot="note">
      The businesses we map are running <strong>six to eleven</strong> separate systems,
      with two to four people spending part of every day moving data between them by hand.
    </Fragment>
  </Section>

  <Section
    id="how"
    eyebrow="§ 02 — How it works"
    heading="One line through everything you run."
    headingWidth={18}
  >
    <p class="lead" style="max-width:56ch">
      We don’t replace your tools. We build the layer that runs through them — so the data
      moves on its own and your team looks in one place.
    </p>

    <Figure caption="Fig. 2 — The thread, drawn">
      <Fig2ThreadDiagram />
    </Figure>

    <StepRow />
  </Section>

  <Section
    id="services"
    eyebrow="§ 03 — Services"
    heading="Four kinds of work, one underlying job."
    headingWidth={16}
    noteLabel="Engagement shape"
    docGap={44}
  >
    <p class="lead" style="max-width:52ch">
      Most engagements are a combination. The map tells us which.
    </p>

    <Fragment slot="note">
      Fixed-scope projects with a fixed price, or a monthly retainer for ongoing build and
      support. No hourly billing, no change-order games.
    </Fragment>

    <ServiceList slot="after" />
  </Section>

  <Section
    id="products"
    eyebrow="§ 04 — Products"
    heading="Some of it we’ve already built."
    headingWidth={18}
    noteLabel="Note"
  >
    <p class="lead" style="max-width:54ch">
      Where the same problem kept showing up, we turned the solution into a product. Buy it
      outright or subscribe — either way it’s the same software we’d build you.
    </p>

    <Fragment slot="note">
      Every product includes the source. If you outgrow us, you leave with what you paid
      for.
    </Fragment>

    <ProductGrid slot="after" />
  </Section>

  <Section
    id="work"
    eyebrow="§ 05 — Work"
    heading="Every project ships with its plate."
    headingWidth={18}
  >
    <p class="lead" style="max-width:56ch">
      We document what we built and why, in plain English, so the knowledge lives with you
      and not only with us.
    </p>

    <Specimen />
  </Section>

  <Section
    id="about"
    eyebrow="§ 06 — About"
    heading="Built in Hawaiʻi. Useful anywhere."
    headingWidth={17}
    noteLabel="Working with us"
  >
    <p class="txt" style="margin-bottom:16px">
      Thread is a small custom software practice based in Honolulu. We work with businesses
      across the islands and with clients on the mainland who’d rather hire a team that
      answers the phone than a firm that assigns them an account manager.
    </p>
    <p class="txt" style="margin-bottom:16px">
      Being here shapes how we work. Island businesses tend to run lean, on tools chosen
      years ago for good reasons, with no appetite for ripping everything out and starting
      over. That constraint turned out to be the right way to build software for anyone.
    </p>
    <p class="txt">
      The name is the whole idea: the connecting thread that runs through everything a
      business already uses, and turns a pile of separate tools into one thing you can
      actually operate.
    </p>

    <Fragment slot="note">
      Time zones are real. We keep overlapping hours with the mainland West Coast and East
      Coast, and we answer within one business day. Most clients never need a meeting that
      isn’t a demo.
    </Fragment>
  </Section>

  <ContactSection />
  <Footer />
</Base>
